# Regression: opening, DRAGGING ACROSS, and closing the game menu must leave the top strip
# AND the scene pristine. QFG1 target, save slot 1 (room 300: the Game/Action/Information
# dropdowns extend deep into the scene over the green half-timbered Hero's Tale Inn at rows
# ~30..110 and over the Sheriff building roof at rows ~20..95).
#
# Two round-2 Roger defects this pins (both on the mouse-menu path):
#   #1 stuck menu-title strip — SCI closes the mouse menu via bitsRestore of the full menu
#      strip (reverting the NATIVE pixels to the score banner) with NO follow-up
#      kernelDrawStatus, so the enhanced strip stayed stuck on "File Game Action
#      Information" while native showed the banner (SBS-confirmed). After close the strip
#      must revert to "Quest for Glory I [score ...]": m-open (titles) must differ from
#      m-after over the strip band (presenceDiff), AND m-after must equal the pre-menu
#      banner m-before over the strip band (sameRunDiff). The banner text does not animate.
#   #2 scene-deep dropdown stamp — a closed dropdown must not leave a tracked non-enhanced
#      pixel stamp (priority-255, NOT healed by mouse-over) in the scene. The dropdowns
#      dragged over the left Inn wall AND the Sheriff roof; after close + mouse-over both
#      bands must match the pre-menu scene (m-before ~ m-afterhover), left of the animating
#      ego/NPC. A real stamp there is thousands of full-width px.
#
# The SCI0 frozen mouse-menu loop DOES observe injected MOUSEMOVE events, so a press-hold +
# `move` across titles switches dropdowns and dragging down into a dropdown highlights its
# items — verified (drag-proof: File->Game dropdown switch + item highlight; the Information
# dropdown drag opens deep over the roof). The one caveat: a slow `snap` (grabOverlay ~1s)
# runs inside the driver's poll and re-anchors the schedule so following moves stay spaced —
# do NOT interleave `snap` between drag `move`s expecting real-time steering (park + settle,
# then snap AFTER the drag has registered).
#
# `snap` (grabOverlay at execution time), NOT `capture`: the composited cursor is parked off
# both checked bands (bottom-right) before each grab, and snap grabs AFTER the park move has
# been presented, so the boot-position arrow cannot inject cursor diff over a checked band.
wait 4000
move 300 185
wait 1000
snap m-before
# --- press File, DRAG right across the whole bar so each deep dropdown opens over the
#     Inn wall (Game/Action) and the roof (Information), then drag DOWN into the deepest
#     one and back up, and release outside to cancel-close (no menu item executed) ---
mousedown 15 2
wait 500
move 55 2
wait 500
move 130 2
wait 500
move 215 2
wait 500
snap m-open
# drag down into the Information dropdown (deep over the roof) then back onto the bar
move 215 45
wait 500
move 215 2
wait 500
# release right of Information on the bar (harmless cancel-close)
mouseup 310 2
wait 1400
move 300 185
wait 1000
snap m-after
# move the mouse THROUGH the dropdowns' former scene footprint (Inn wall AND roof), then
# park off-band: a real stamp is priority-255 and is NOT healed by mouse-over, so it shows.
move 40 34
wait 300
move 120 60
wait 300
move 210 40
wait 300
move 260 35
wait 300
move 300 185
wait 1000
snap m-afterhover
wait 300
quit
